     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is double the maximum recommended metformin dose. That maximum is 2,550 mg/day, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual 1,000 mg per-dose ceiling. At that dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is significant, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses (for example, 850 mg twice daily)\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, please confirm. I can enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
